From 06954a3af743e9cc559370ca763ba1e0bd92522f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:02:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH qemu-server 2/4] vga: add option to export the display over
 D-Bus

QEMU's D-Bus display hands the guest scanout -- including the GL
scanout of virtio-gl as DMA-BUF -- to an external consumer and takes
keyboard, mouse, clipboard and audio from it.  It is meant for
consoles that do more than VNC, such as a hardware-encoded video
stream to the browser.

Add a 'dbus' flag to the VGA option that adds

  -display dbus,p2p=yes,gl=on|off[,rendernode=...]

In peer-to-peer mode no D-Bus daemon is involved: a consumer gets
attached per connection through QMP (getfd + add_client).  GL is used
for virtio-gl, which then no longer needs egl-headless.

With GL, QEMU does not allow VNC or SPICE next to the D-Bus display
("Display vnc is incompatible with the GL context"), so a virtio-gl VM
with 'dbus' has neither of those consoles; vncproxy and spiceproxy say
so instead of failing to connect.  Other display types keep them.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
